///|
/// multibase's `base256emoji` alphabet, indexed by byte value:
/// https://github.com/multiformats/multibase/blob/master/rfcs/Base256Emoji.md
///
/// One character per byte value, so the encoding is a substitution and nothing
/// more — no bit packing, no padding, no length rule. It is here because it is in
/// the table, and because it is the one entry that makes a library prove it can
/// hold a character that is not one UTF-16 code unit.
